# Figma Design System Rules

This document defines how to translate Figma designs into code for **Electric Maybe Shopify themes** (Liquid templates, Tailwind CSS v4, native JavaScript web components). Figma MCP output is typically React + Tailwind; treat that as design reference only and implement using this theme’s stack and conventions.

**Color work:** read `theme-color-modes.mdc` first. Figma SSOT is the **7-collection** set below. Brand vertical goes on **`<html>`**; section tone on the **section root**; component tokens map to **atoms**. `_styles/` may lag — discover exact names before coding. Never emit arbitrary hex or Brand ramps as Liquid classes.

---

## 1. Design System Structure

### 1.1 Figma variable SSOT (7 collections)

EISCO Main variables (~280 vars). This is the **structure** to match — not a dump of every variable. `_styles/` file names vary; grep before coding.

| Collection | Modes | What it holds | Liquid / CSS use |
|---|---|---|---|
| `01.01 Theme/Primitives` | Mode 1 | Spacing, text, rounded ≈ **stock Tailwind** | TW-native (`--spacing()`, default theme). Do **not** re-declare every `--spacing-8`. Figma half-steps (`0,5`, `9xl-1`, `12rem`) are **cleanup** — do not invent them in Liquid |
| `01.02 Theme/Brand` | `education` \| `industrial` | Fonts; `color/accent/50–950`; `color/brand/*`; `color/neutral/*`; radii | **Brand vertical on `<html>`** (`brand-educational` / `brand-education` or `brand-industrial` — discover exact class). One class rebinds Brand CSS variables for the whole tree. Never Liquid `text-neutral-400` / `bg-accent-700` |
| `02.01 Base/Sizes` | `lg` \| `md` \| `default` | Layout density; `max-width/sm\|base\|lg\|xl\|2xl` aliasing `spacing/*`; px/py/gap/height/icon/text-size | May **override stock Tailwind** (`max-w-sm`, etc.). Grep `_styles/02_base/*sizes*` — do not assume stock values. Responsive `md:` / `lg:`, not hard `px` |
| `02.02 Base/Colors` | `primary` \| `secondary` \| `muted` \| `accent` \| `contrast` \| `elevated` | Semantic roles (aliases into Brand) | **Section tone** on the section root; children use roles below |
| `02.03 Base/Alphacolors` | — | Legacy `0-*` overlays | **Cleanup / legacy.** Do not teach as the primary API |
| `03.01 Components/Sizes` | `lg` \| `base` \| `sm` | Button / input density | **Atoms** (`a--button`, inputs) — not flat `button/height` utilities |
| `03.02 Components/Colors` | `primary` \| `secondary` | Component color + state opacities | Atom classes / data attributes composed from Base tokens |

**Everything from `01.02` onward is customized** — discover from `_styles/` (and Figma when scaffolding). `01.01` is the TW-native exception.

**Two axes**

1. **Brand vertical** (`01.02 Theme/Brand`) — **one class on `<html>`** (`brand-educational` or `brand-industrial`; accept `brand-education` if that is what `_styles/` / `theme.liquid` ships). Rebinds accent/neutral ramps, fonts, radii for the whole tree. Not a section class.
2. **Section tone** (`02.02 Base/Colors`) — mode class on the **section root**. New Figma-driven themes: six tones, single `accent` (not `accent-1|2|3`). Children stay semantic.

**Older `_styles/`:** some themes still ship `color-schema-accent-1|2|3` and omit `elevated`. Discover and use what exists. Do not invent missing utilities.

**Semantic roles** (`02.02 Base/Colors` → Tailwind when scaffolded in `_styles/`):

- **bg:** `surface`, `subtle`, `emphasis`, `accent`, `accent-sec`
- **text:** `primary`, `secondary`, `accent`, `on-accent`, `on-accent-sec`
- **border:** `primary`, `secondary`, `tertiary`, `accent`, `on-accent`, `on-accent-sec`

Map Figma → Liquid: brand on `<html>`, tone on the section, then these role names on children **when `_styles/` defines them**. Missing roles (`text-accent`, `bg-accent-sec`, `border-tertiary`, `border-accent`, `elevated`) need a theme token-scaffold PR — not hex, not invented classes.

**Overridden utilities:** do not assume stock Tailwind for `max-w-*` or other roles listed in `_styles/02_base/*sizes*` (px, py, gap, height, icon, text-size). Grep first.

**Components → atoms:** `03.01` / `03.02` are the button/input matrix. Use `{% render 'a--button', ... %}` (and input atoms) with size/variant params. Do not invent `button/height` utilities. If atoms do not implement the matrix, that is a theme `_styles` gap — do not fake with hex.

**Rules**

- IMPORTANT: Never hardcode hex/hsl in Liquid or CSS (`text-[#d1d1d1]`, raw `#fff`). Use semantic utilities under the active color mode (`theme-color-modes.mdc`).
- Spacing: `01.01` is TW-native; `02.01` may override — grep `_styles/`, never arbitrary `px` or Figma half-steps.
- Typography must use this theme’s font utilities (Brand + Primitive text) confirmed in `_styles/`.

### 1.2 Component Library

**Where components live**

- **Sections (full-width, schema-driven):** `sections/*.liquid` — e.g. `sections/s--hero-banner.liquid`, `sections/s--featured-collection.liquid`.
- **Snippets (reusable UI):**  
  - Atoms: `snippets/a--*.liquid` (e.g. `a--icon.liquid`, `a--button.liquid`, `a--input.liquid`).  
  - Molecules: `snippets/m--*.liquid` (e.g. `m--product-card.liquid`, `m--accordion.liquid`, `m--modal.liquid`).  
  - Feature-specific: `snippets/product--*.liquid`, `snippets/cart--*.liquid`, `snippets/header--*.liquid`, etc.
- **Web components (JS):** `_scripts/*.js` — e.g. `electric-modal.js`, `electric-slider.js`, `electric-disclosure.js`. Reference implementation: `_scripts/electric-modal.js`.

**Architecture**

- No React/Vue. UI is Liquid (sections + snippets) plus native JS web components.
- New UI from Figma: prefer adding or composing existing snippets/sections; add new snippets/sections only when no fit exists.
- Sections must have a valid `{% schema %}` and semantic HTML; snippets must have LiquidDoc `{%- doc -%}` and follow `.config/ai/rules/snippets.mdc` and `.config/ai/rules/liquid.mdc`.

### 1.3 Frameworks & Libraries

- **Templating:** Liquid only (Shopify theme).
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS v4. Entry: `_styles/main.css` (imports Tailwind, tokens, component CSS). Compiled output: `assets/style.css`.
- **Script:** Native JS only (no React/Vue). Web components with `#` private fields, AbortController for listeners, JSDoc; see `.config/ai/rules/javascript-standards.mdc`.
- **Build:** Tailwind processes `_styles/main.css`; content sources (for class scanning) are listed in `_styles/main.css` (`@source` for layout, blocks, sections, snippets, templates, assets).

### 1.4 Asset Management

- **Theme assets:** `assets/` — CSS, JS, and static files. Reference in Liquid with `{{ 'filename.css' | asset_url }}` or `{{ 'filename.js' | asset_url }}`.
- **Images:** Use Shopify CDN via filters: `{{ image | image_url: width: N }}` for responsive widths; use `srcset` where appropriate (see existing snippets/sections).
- **Icons:** Do not add new icon packages. Use the icon system below (inline SVG via `a--icon` or assets from Figma MCP when provided).
- **Figma MCP assets:** If the Figma MCP server returns a localhost (or other) URL for an image/SVG, use that source directly. Do not replace with placeholders when a real URL is given.
- Store any downloaded assets from Figma in `assets/` and reference via `asset_url`.

### 1.5 Icon System

- **Definition:** Icons are inline SVGs in `snippets/a--icon.liquid`, selected by name via `icon: 'name'`.
- **Usage:** `{% render 'a--icon', icon: 'search', size: 'base', class: '...' %}`. Parameters: `icon` (required), `class`, `color`, `size` (xxs|xs|sm|base|lg|xl), `width`/`height`, `stroke`, `animate`, `aria_label`, `aria_hidden`, etc. See LiquidDoc in `a--icon.liquid`.
- **Naming:** kebab-case (e.g. `chevron-d`, `arrow-r-up`, `circle-arrow-r`). Add new icons in the same file as new `when 'name'` branches; keep `fill="none"` and use `{{ color }}` or `currentColor` for strokes/fills.
- **Sizing:** Prefer `size` (uses `--height-icon-*` tokens); or `width`/`height` for explicit dimensions. Stroke from size or `stroke` param (`stroke-sm`, `stroke-base`, etc.).

### 1.6 Styling Approach

- **Methodology:** Utility-first with Tailwind. Custom utilities and theme in `_styles/main.css` and `_styles/02_base/*.css`, `_styles/01_theme/*.css`.
- **CRITICAL — Static classes only:** Tailwind scans at build time; Liquid runs on the server. Do not build class names with Liquid variables (e.g. no `duration-{{ x }}`, `text-{{ color }}`). Use fixed classes or conditionals that output full class names, e.g. `{% if size == 'sm' %}text-sm{% else %}text-base{% endif %}`.
- **Responsive:** Mobile-first. Use `md:` and `lg:` prefixes. Figma `02.01 Base/Sizes` modes (`lg` | `md` | `default`) become responsive utilities, not hard `px`. **Do not assume stock Tailwind** for `max-w-*` (or px/py/gap/height/icon/text-size) if `_styles/02_base/*sizes*` redefines them. Component density (`03.01`) is atom params (`lg` | `base` | `sm`), not one-off utilities.
- **Semantic tokens in Tailwind:** Brand class on `<html>`, section tone on the section root, children use only Base/Colors semantic roles from `_styles/`. Do not invent tokens, paste Figma hex, or use Brand ramps as classes. See `theme-color-modes.mdc`.
- **Custom component CSS:** Add in `_styles/` (e.g. `_styles/atoms/`, `_styles/molecules/`) and import from `_styles/main.css`.

### 1.7 Project Structure

```
_layout/theme.liquid     # Main layout
_scripts/                # Web components and utilities (native JS)
_styles/                 # Tailwind entry, tokens, component CSS
  main.css
  01_theme/              # Figma 01.01 Primitives + 01.02 Brand (paths vary)
  02_base/               # Figma 02.01 Sizes, 02.02 Colors, 02.03 Alphacolors (legacy)
  …                      # Figma 03.01 / 03.02 component tokens when scaffolded
  atoms/, molecules/, core/
assets/                  # Compiled CSS/JS and static assets
sections/                # Liquid section files
snippets/                # Reusable Liquid snippets (a--*, m--*, etc.)
templates/               # Page templates
locales/                 # Translation files
config/                  # Theme settings
```

- **Feature organization:** Sections and snippets are named by feature or type (e.g. `product--main`, `cart--drawer`, `s--hero-banner`, `m--product-card`). Follow existing naming (prefix + `--` + descriptor).

